# =============================================================================
# Docker build context exclusions
#
# THE FIRST BLOCK IS A SECURITY CONTROL, NOT AN OPTIMISATION.
#
# Everything in the build context is readable by every layer of the build, and
# anything COPYed in survives in the image even if a later layer deletes it.
# `.env` holds ENCRYPTION_KEY — the master key for the credential vault — and
# an image is a file that gets pushed to a registry and pulled by anyone with
# access to it.
#
# `.gitignore` already excludes `.env` from git. It does NOT exclude it from a
# Docker build: the build context is the directory on disk, not the git index.
# Two separate mechanisms, and both have to be right.
# =============================================================================

.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
local/
backups/

# --- Never copy host node_modules -------------------------------------------
# They contain binaries resolved for Windows. The image installs its own from
# the same lockfile, with the Linux platform resolved instead.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# --- Build output, rebuilt inside the image ----------------------------------
# Copying host output would ship whatever happened to be on a developer's disk
# rather than what the lockfile reproducibly produces.
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
.turbo
**/.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- The web app ------------------------------------------------------------
# Its SOURCE is not needed: this image is the API, and the web app deploys to
# Vercel separately.
#
# Its `package.json` IS needed and is deliberately kept. `apps/web` is a member
# of the pnpm workspace and appears in `pnpm-lock.yaml`; with the manifest
# missing, `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` treats the lockfile as out of date
# and fails the build. Verified against the lockfile rather than assumed.
apps/web/*
!apps/web/package.json

# --- Not needed to build or run the API -------------------------------------
# `tests/` is not a workspace member (the workspace is `apps/*` + `packages/*`),
# so excluding it cannot affect dependency resolution. Test files are already
# excluded by apps/api/tsconfig.build.json.
.git
.github
.vercel
docs
tests
**/*.test.ts
**/*.spec.ts
coverage
.vscode
.idea
*.log
README.md
